  "surprise": "Statement-modelling auxiliary loss (next-token CE on the theorem-statement tokens at weight 0.1, pretraining only; handoff model byte-identical to 153 at 9,557,760 params) on 153-claude scored 670/670/665 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 153's 676/700/685: exact means 668.33 vs 687.00, -18.67, paired -6/-30/-20, every seed below its counterpart, inside the registered -40..+40 range but below its central +6. Discard. No keep landed during the run (161-fable2 SwiGLU 635, 162-fable tail curriculum 633, 163-claude repeat-6line 665 were all discarded), so the incumbent stays 153. The term was free and did NOT hurt the proof fit, so the fit falsifiers did not fire: steps 4532/4473/4336 (mean 4447 vs 153's 4503, -1.2%; registered 4,300-4,750; 717/677/688 steps at 60 s vs the bench's 714), 4.0/3.95/3.83 epochs; final proof val 0.0880/0.0828/0.0818 (153: 0.0883/0.0869/0.0888), minima 0.0732/0.0798/0.0806 at 165/135/240 s, final train 0.0543/0.0537/0.0506; post-pretrain held-out greedy 0.978/0.977/0.968 (153: 0.9675/0.967/0.968), i.e. equal or slightly better on every fit diagnostic. Prediction miss: prompt_loss ended at 0.397/0.406/0.410 nats, BELOW the registered 0.6-2.5 (1.2-1.35 at 30 s, 0.48-0.50 at 60 s, 0.42-0.45 at 120 s, then flat); Lean statements are far more predictable than assumed (rigid syntax, atoms shared between hypotheses and goal), though the >= 5x ratio to the proof train loss held (7.3-8.1x at 300 s). The mechanism check FAILED: round-1 RL targets solved 746/514/624 (mean 628 vs 153's 766/747/694 = 736; registered 690-870, two seeds below it; the < 620-on-two-seeds falsifier missed by 4 on seed 2) with round-1 sample acc 0.280/0.110/0.152 (153: 0.27/0.28/0.21), so the handoff sampler was at or below 153's on every seed despite the equal-or-better in-distribution fit. Round-4 RL-solved 1154/1139/1166 (mean 1153 vs 1172; inside the registered 1,130-1,210 but below 153 on every seed), round-4 acc 0.738/0.721/0.742; eval L* 11/12/11; eval/round-4 ratio 0.581/0.588/0.570 (153: 0.584/0.599/0.575), so the transfer ratio is unchanged and the whole deficit is the RL start and trajectory. Post-RL held-out greedy 0.992/0.993/0.991. Totals 1783/1981/1649 s (seed 1 sampled slowest, 176-290 samples/s; registered 1,600-1,950, one seed over by 31 s). Reading (hypothesis, not shown): the statement term buys fit on the <= 6-line training statements without buying anything the T=0.8 sampler needs on 7-14-line targets, and Muon's orthogonalized direction gave that objective a growing share of late updates (0.1 x 0.4 nats against a 0.05-nat proof loss), so the proof-generation features got fewer effective steps at unchanged loss; equal greedy on short proofs plus worse round-1 on long targets is the same length-transfer signature as 157-fable3 and 161-fable3, both data-side changes that also left the fit intact. Follow-ups in this lane would need a new hypothesis: goal-only supervision (the forward-inference part of the statement, not the hypotheses) is the untested half of the mechanism; a smaller weight is just a nudge.",
